LapisLazuli: notices

This file says where the repository's content came from and lists the third-party material it
keeps, with the basis for keeping each item. Third-party material stays under its owner's terms or
under the quotation basis given here. The repository's own license does not relicense it.

1. Where the content came from

Most of the knowledge in src/skills/ and src/shared/ was migrated from the author's previous
repository, design-and-frontend, which is not part of this repository. tools/migration-map.yaml and
tools/reference-provenance.yaml record which files became which. Sources named "memo:" in
src/shared/slop/rules.yaml are the author's own memos on text, layout, color, and structure. They
are unpublished and kept outside this repository.

The previous repository's text was written by its author and the author's agents, with research and
reference material mixed in. The migration rewrote that material or left it out. On 2026-09-30 the
published text was compared with the previous repository and with the standards, guidelines, and
agent-skill repositories it draws on, looking for shared passages of twelve or more words (Korean:
twenty or more syllables) and for lists and tables in the same order. Apart from the quotations in
section 2, no such passage was found.

