3. Recorded catalog test data

tests/fixtures/catalog/ holds test data shaped like responses from open font catalogs, recorded
on 2026-09-26 and trimmed. Only facts stayed as recorded (family names, ids and slugs, categories,
subsets, weights, axis ranges, license identifiers). Every value a catalog curates or measures is
synthetic. tests/fixtures/catalog/README.md gives each file's source and the license of the
original.

- google-fonts/: shaped like https://fonts.google.com/metadata/fonts and the google/fonts
  repository on GitHub (tags/all/families.csv and git trees). No data license is stated for the
  metadata or the tags. The repository's README gives the font licenses by directory: OFL-1.1 in
  ofl/, Apache-2.0 in apache/, UFL-1.0 in ufl/.
- fontshare/: shaped like https://api.fontshare.com/v2/fonts. Names, slugs, and license types stay.
  The fonts are under the ITF Free Font License; no license for the API data was found.
- fontsource/: shaped like https://api.fontsource.org/v1/fonts. Ids, family names, subsets, weights,
  and SPDX license ids stay. The Fontsource repository is MIT (Copyright (c) 2024 Ayuhito).
- sandoll/ and anshim/: hand-written samples shaped like pages of sandollcloud.com and
  gongu.copyright.or.kr. They keep short labels, font names, and license holders. Their robots.txt
  files are hand-written descriptions of the rules, not copies.

Family names can be trademarks. They name the fonts and nothing more. No font file is in the
repository.

4. Projects that shaped ideas and vocabulary

These projects informed the plan fields, the slop rule families, and the structure of the skills.
No text was copied from them. Their licenses are given so their terms are easy to find.

- Impeccable, https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable (Apache-2.0): surface modes, task vocabulary,
  audit and improvement patterns.
- taste-skill, https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill (MIT): brief inference, qualitative dials,
  keeping decisions when redesigning.
- better-ui skills, https://github.com/jakubkrehel/skills (MIT): optical alignment, surfaces,
  interaction polish.
- Vercel Web Interface Guidelines, https://github.com/vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines (MIT):
  browser behavior review.
- Anthropic frontend-design skill, https://github.com/anthropics/skills (Apache-2.0):
  subject-grounded direction.

tools/reference-provenance.yaml names the standards and other works behind each skill reference.

5. Names and marks

Names of standards, products, fonts, services, and companies appear only to identify them. They
belong to their owners. The repository states no proprietary color standard's values, and lazuli
stores only codes and links for those standards.
